(2483764, 337973, 14414, '<td valign="top"><b><i>Composition </i></b> <br/>composition is good, in terms of the "baghead" in the upper left third, and the laptop in the bottom right. The home/offic-ey environment makes it a more cluttered composition though, especially with the detail in the blinds.<br/> <br/><b><i>Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc) </i></b> <br/>wb seems a little off, but exposure and focus seem good. You may have been able to isolate the subject from the b/g more with a shallower dof though<br/> <br/><b><i>Post-processing </i></b> <br/>I''d like to see a little more contrast in it, to make it pop more and be less snapshotty<br/> <br/><b><i>Message/atmosphere portrayed </i></b> <br/>Well, you did kinda bring it upon yourself with that title! :P Although  the paper bag fits, another way of "hiding" from your score may have been better, so as to make your expression visible and give more emotion.<br/> <br/><b><i>Meeting the challenge </i></b> <br/>Yeah, sure<br/> <br/><b><i>My personal opinion </i></b> <br/>I wouldn''t have expected this to score very high, just because its  quite a familiar idea - not necessarily exactly that idea, but in terms of comments on scores/people at laptops etc. Would have needed an extra creative something to bring it further<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-05 05:16:46.</i></td>', 'Composition  composition is good, in terms of the "baghead" in the upper left third, and the laptop in the bottom right. The home/offic-ey environment makes it a more cluttered composition though, especially with the detail in the blinds. Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc)  wb seems a little off, but exposure and focus seem good. You may have been able to isolate the subject from the b/g more with a shallower dof though Post-processing  I''d like to see a little more contrast in it, to make it pop more and be less snapshotty Message/atmosphere portrayed  Well, you did kinda bring it upon yourself with that title! :P Although  the paper bag fits, another way of "hiding" from your score may have been better, so as to make your expression visible and give more emotion. Meeting the challenge  Yeah, sure My personal opinion  I wouldn''t have expected this to score very high, just because its  quite a familiar idea - not necessarily exactly that idea, but in terms of comments on scores/people at laptops etc. Would have needed an extra creative something to bring it further', '2006-06-04 16:33:07.000000', '2006-06-05 06:16:46.000000', 0),
(2483826, 337358, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>You got what you want .... a pile of controversy :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The fountain hits thirds .. the top of the house hits thirds .. but it still feels centred ... not sure why ...<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Does it or not ... really I am from NZ .. and it doesn''t do much for me ... but in your country it may. <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Nice Colours and natural light .. both work well .. .also a good sharp picture.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Do something that says something to all .. .the problem is that this site is not made up of mainly americans .. so it doesn''t say much to a lot of people ... and those it does it seems you offended some of them.  <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I like this as an architechture shot ... which is currently voting and think it would have done ok in there.  But is a personal statement and I think worked well for that.  Keep it up .. I personally like challenging peoples thinking too.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: You got what you want .... a pile of controversy :) Composition: The fountain hits thirds .. the top of the house hits thirds .. but it still feels centred ... not sure why ... Subject: Does it or not ... really I am from NZ .. and it doesn''t do much for me ... but in your country it may.  Technical (Colour and light): Nice Colours and natural light .. both work well .. .also a good sharp picture. To grow its vote?: Do something that says something to all .. .the problem is that this site is not made up of mainly americans .. so it doesn''t say much to a lot of people ... and those it does it seems you offended some of them.   Summary: I like this as an architechture shot ... which is currently voting and think it would have done ok in there.  But is a personal statement and I think worked well for that.  Keep it up .. I personally like challenging peoples thinking too. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 16:59:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483848, 337752, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting composition ... nice lines .... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The leading lines in this picture are great ... your eye goes up the line of the tree and gets dragged further into the picture .. unfortunately they end at the sidewalk and that doesn''t do the shot justice.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. and does so with gusto.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The DOF is a little shallow ... that the base of the tree is totally blurred means you can''t see that it is ''broken'' off persay.  It is also really dark ... maybe a little fill flash would have helpted ... or seeing that the path is shiny a different angle may have allowed more natural light.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about the angles of the shot .. take many pictures and when reviewing and selecting your entry think about how others will see your picture .. and the questions that they will ask.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great work .. second entry and improving .. you are doing well.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting composition ... nice lines ....  Composition: The leading lines in this picture are great ... your eye goes up the line of the tree and gets dragged further into the picture .. unfortunately they end at the sidewalk and that doesn''t do the shot justice. Subject: Meets the challenge .. and does so with gusto. Technical (Colour and light): The DOF is a little shallow ... that the base of the tree is totally blurred means you can''t see that it is ''broken'' off persay.  It is also really dark ... maybe a little fill flash would have helpted ... or seeing that the path is shiny a different angle may have allowed more natural light. To grow its vote?: Think about the angles of the shot .. take many pictures and when reviewing and selecting your entry think about how others will see your picture .. and the questions that they will ask. Summary: Great work .. second entry and improving .. you are doing well. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 17:17:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483914, 336141, 27686, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone, this was my 1st challenge. Everyone is correct they were too perfectly placed. I should have done what you all said and I thankyou for the input.</td>', 'Thanks everyone, this was my 1st challenge. Everyone is correct they were too perfectly placed. I should have done what you all said and I thankyou for the input.', '2006-06-04 18:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483920, 336135, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I am good at multiple choice .. its the one type of test where learning my rote works well.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>There are so many elements in this picture .. and I think they are all needed .. the broken pencils and the tests and note books .... but they don''t help to take it to the next level .... I think that having a search on the rule of thirds may help when setting up this kind of shoot.  This is more learning and more rules .. but there are only a few in photography .. and they all help.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge, but I am not sure what the title adds to it.  I did not feel this was a failure to confirm ... it was a failure to learn by that method ... not many learn by multiple choice.  I would think that conforming was another issue ... oh well failure as with success is self determined .. and it is about getting the right message across.... so its just about trying and finding what works for you.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I think this works well .. the DOF is good ... not being able to read the papers beyond the f is good .. and lighting seems to work ok.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how others see the shot ... take a look at the rules of photography as these also help.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good work .. a nice improvement on your first entry ... you are going in leaps and bounds.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: I am good at multiple choice .. its the one type of test where learning my rote works well. Composition: There are so many elements in this picture .. and I think they are all needed .. the broken pencils and the tests and note books .... but they don''t help to take it to the next level .... I think that having a search on the rule of thirds may help when setting up this kind of shoot.  This is more learning and more rules .. but there are only a few in photography .. and they all help. Subject: Meets the challenge, but I am not sure what the title adds to it.  I did not feel this was a failure to confirm ... it was a failure to learn by that method ... not many learn by multiple choice.  I would think that conforming was another issue ... oh well failure as with success is self determined .. and it is about getting the right message across.... so its just about trying and finding what works for you. Technical (Colour and light): I think this works well .. the DOF is good ... not being able to read the papers beyond the f is good .. and lighting seems to work ok. To grow its vote?: Think about how others see the shot ... take a look at the rules of photography as these also help. Summary: Good work .. a nice improvement on your first entry ... you are going in leaps and bounds. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:05:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484006, 337130, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I don''t understand how the title relates .. until I read your comments .. so will base the critique on what you were trying to achieve and how to best meet that as well as the image you created.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Background is so very important and from this angle the backgroun detracts from the actual image .. something flat may have helped here rather than the heavy texture.  do a search on ''rule of thirds" I have learn lots about composition using this rule . .. also the golden triange .. and leading lines.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Not as it is pictured .. but your concept does - you just haven''t pulled it off.  <br/> <br/>I think that the blue you have used does not work .. and the angle of the shot detracts from the boot and the rose as both are almost entirely lost in this picture.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The imaage does not appear sharp.  The flaring off the water is a little bit of an issue but the colour blue has basically killed the shot.  It is a little too bright t depict the sadness.  A naturally dying rose in the boot from the side wtih a mild tope angle on it may have actually portrayed what you are looking for and created the emotion without the need or colour saturation.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how others will see the shot, and the impression it will leave on them.  Take into account that things like failure are self determined and that people will judge on their own experience.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>you did ok .. keep it up you will do better i am sure in future.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: I don''t understand how the title relates .. until I read your comments .. so will base the critique on what you were trying to achieve and how to best meet that as well as the image you created. Composition: Background is so very important and from this angle the backgroun detracts from the actual image .. something flat may have helped here rather than the heavy texture.  do a search on ''rule of thirds" I have learn lots about composition using this rule . .. also the golden triange .. and leading lines. Subject: Not as it is pictured .. but your concept does - you just haven''t pulled it off.   I think that the blue you have used does not work .. and the angle of the shot detracts from the boot and the rose as both are almost entirely lost in this picture. Technical (Colour and light): The imaage does not appear sharp.  The flaring off the water is a little bit of an issue but the colour blue has basically killed the shot.  It is a little too bright t depict the sadness.  A naturally dying rose in the boot from the side wtih a mild tope angle on it may have actually portrayed what you are looking for and created the emotion without the need or colour saturation. To grow its vote?: Think about how others will see the shot, and the impression it will leave on them.  Take into account that things like failure are self determined and that people will judge on their own experience. Summary: you did ok .. keep it up you will do better i am sure in future. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:56:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484136, 337066, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Its a pity I am an ex-smoker .. I can still smell the stuff.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Works for this picture.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge well and truly.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Great colour and good use of DOF ... I like that the fags in the background are out of focus as this gives a great impression of trying to quit and  failing.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>hard to say .. this type of shot works for some and not others ... <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think this is a great second entry .. you have a good eye .. keep using it.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Its a pity I am an ex-smoker .. I can still smell the stuff. Composition: Works for this picture. Subject: meets the challenge well and truly. Technical (Colour and light): Great colour and good use of DOF ... I like that the fags in the background are out of focus as this gives a great impression of trying to quit and  failing. To grow its vote?: hard to say .. this type of shot works for some and not others ...  Summary: I think this is a great second entry .. you have a good eye .. keep using it. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:51:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484157, 338146, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>There are so many contradictory comments on this image, it really is up to you who if any your listen to.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Yup .. lonely and all alone .. but the title is what i have to look at t make the story complete.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like this composition.  It works... I think in order to really make the image i would have turned the models head and place it resting on the hand ... this puts across a slight destitute feel.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge, but the title does help it get there.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Lovely .. I like the siluoette .. I like the colours in the sky.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how you use a model to convery what you are looking for, otherwise it can look just like a lucky snapshot.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great work .. and well done.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. There are so many contradictory comments on this image, it really is up to you who if any your listen to. First Impression - the most important one: Yup .. lonely and all alone .. but the title is what i have to look at t make the story complete. Composition: I like this composition.  It works... I think in order to really make the image i would have turned the models head and place it resting on the hand ... this puts across a slight destitute feel. Subject: Meets the challenge, but the title does help it get there. Technical (Colour and light): Lovely .. I like the siluoette .. I like the colours in the sky. To grow its vote?: Think about how you use a model to convery what you are looking for, otherwise it can look just like a lucky snapshot. Summary: Great work .. and well done. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:03:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484265, 336036, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Size is important when creating an image, and working to the maximum size is best .. . try and get at least 640 on the long side to maximise the potential of a shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Interesting woody and woody almost both of thirds.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I really love this shot ... it is only the size that let it down to me.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I like the creation of using the foil or the background of the shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about size, think about impact and light.  Think about the rule of thirds (google it) .. this will keep you on the way. <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great first entry I am impressed .. imagination and an eye.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Size is important when creating an image, and working to the maximum size is best .. . try and get at least 640 on the long side to maximise the potential of a shot. Composition: Interesting woody and woody almost both of thirds. Subject: I really love this shot ... it is only the size that let it down to me. Technical (Colour and light): I like the creation of using the foil or the background of the shot. To grow its vote?: Think about size, think about impact and light.  Think about the rule of thirds (google it) .. this will keep you on the way.  Summary: Great first entry I am impressed .. imagination and an eye. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:55:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484274, 337881, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>outside your norm and you still got top 15 ... you are good.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The player is centred but the action is all around so this really does work.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>So subjective really, failure is really self determined.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>lovely colours and a good sharp action shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Take not of what is below include the ball next time (heheh)<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great work .. and well done ... not bad placing for a placeholder.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: outside your norm and you still got top 15 ... you are good. Composition: The player is centred but the action is all around so this really does work. Subject: So subjective really, failure is really self determined. Technical (Colour and light): lovely colours and a good sharp action shot. To grow its vote?: Take not of what is below include the ball next time (heheh) Summary: Great work .. and well done ... not bad placing for a placeholder. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 21:00:09.000000', NULL, 0),
